# Gitleaks allowlist.
#
# One fingerprint per line, each with a dated reason. An entry with no reason is
# not allowed. Nothing is silenced here because it is inconvenient, only because
# the material is permanent in this repository's history AND has been shown to
# be worthless.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why an allowlist rather than a history rewrite.
#
# A rewrite was done on cube-store for its exposed Stripe key and it is
# deliberately not repeated here. Measured there afterwards: GitHub pins every
# pull request's head commit under refs/pull/*, which no force-push can reach,
# so 102 matches stayed fetchable and only GitHub Support can purge them. What
# actually closed that exposure was rotating the key.
#
# So the honest control for permanent history is: neutralise the material, then
# record it. Everything below is neutralised. Every entry says how.
#
# NONE of these files is tracked at the tip or present on disk. The `secrets`
# job in ci.yml enforces that separately and independently, and it is the check
# that caught the second MySQL data directory when a human missed it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

